(Historical Background of the Indian Constitution) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(The Indian Constitution has deep roots in the British colonial) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(administrative architecture. The Regulating Act of 1773 was the first step) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(taken by the British Government to control and regulate the affairs of the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 650 Tm
(East India Company in India.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(Key landmark legislations include the Charter Act of 1833 which centralized) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(legislation under the Governor-General of India \(Lord William Bentinck\), and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(the Government of India Act 1858 which transferred power directly to the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 583 Tm
(British Crown following the 1857 Sepoy Mutiny.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 561 Tm
(The Government of India Act 1935 laid the structural foundation of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(federalism, introducing provincial autonomy, bicameralism in six provinces,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(three legislative lists \(Federal, Provincial, Concurrent\), and the Federal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 516 Tm
(Court.) Tj
