BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(The Preamble to the Indian Constitution is based on the Objective Resolution) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(introduced by Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru on December 13, 1946, and adopted) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(unanimously on January 22, 1947.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 643 Tm
(It declares India to be a SOVEREIGN, SOCIALIST, SECULAR, DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(and secures to all citizens JUSTICE \(social, economic, and political\),) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(LIBERTY of thought, expression, belief, faith and worship, EQUALITY of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(status and opportunity, and FRATERNITY.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(In Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala \(1973\), the Supreme Court held) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 561 Tm
(that the Preamble is an integral part of the Constitution and can be amended) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(under Article 368 without altering the Basic Structure. The 42nd Amendment) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(Act \(1976\) added the words Socialist, Secular, and Integrity.) Tj
ET
