1 0 0 1 50 725 Tm
(Fundamental Rights: Articles 14 to 18 \(Right to Equality\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(Part III of the Constitution \(Articles 12 to 35\) is termed the Magna Carta) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(of India. Fundamental Rights are justifiable, guaranteed against state) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(actions, and defended directly by the Supreme Court under Article 32.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 643 Tm
(Article 14 guarantees Equality before the Law \(British concept, negative in) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(connotation\) and Equal Protection of the Laws \(American concept, positive) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(connotation\). Reasonable classification is permitted, but class legislation) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(is prohibited.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(Article 15 prohibits discrimination on grounds only of religion, race,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 561 Tm
(caste, sex, or place of birth. Article 16 guarantees equality of opportunity) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(in public employment. Article 17 abolishes untouchability, and Article 18) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(abolishes titles except military and academic distinctions.) Tj
ET
