(Right to Freedom: Articles 19 to 22 & Article 21 Expansion) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(Article 19\(1\) guarantees six democratic freedoms: speech and expression,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(assembly peacefully without arms, association/unions/cooperative societies,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(free movement, residence anywhere, and practice of any profession. These are) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 650 Tm
(subject to reasonable restrictions under Article 19\(2\)-\(6\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(Article 20 protects against ex-post facto criminal laws, double jeopardy \(no) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(prosecution twice for same offense\), and self-incrimination.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 591 Tm
(Article 21 declares: No person shall be deprived of his life or personal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(liberty except according to procedure established by law. In Maneka Gandhi) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 561 Tm
(v. Union of India \(1978\), the Supreme Court interpreted this to mean Due) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(Process of Law, ruling that the procedure must be just, fair, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(reasonable. In K.S. Puttaswamy \(2017\), the Right to Privacy was declared an) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 516 Tm
(intrinsic part of Article 21.) Tj
