1 0 0 1 50 725 Tm
(Constitutional Remedies & Writs \(Article 32\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(Dr. B.R. Ambedkar famously called Article 32 the very heart and soul of the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(Constitution. It confers the right to move the Supreme Court by appropriate) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(proceedings for the enforcement of Fundamental Rights.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 643 Tm
(The five prerogative writs are: 1. Habeas Corpus \(To have the body of -) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(against illegal detention\); 2. Mandamus \(We command - compelling a public) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(official to perform statutory duties\); 3. Prohibition \(Issued by higher) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(court to lower court preventing jurisdictional excess\); 4. Certiorari \(To be) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 583 Tm
(certified - quashing orders of inferior courts/tribunals\); 5. Quo-Warranto) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 568 Tm
(\(By what authority - challenging illegal usurpation of public office\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(Article 226 gives High Courts wider writ jurisdiction, extending to) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(fundamental rights as well as ordinary legal rights.) Tj
ET
