/F1 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 725 Tm
(Directive Principles of State Policy \(Articles 36 to 51\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(Borrowed from the Irish Constitution, DPSPs are non-justiciable directives) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(guiding governance towards socio-economic democracy and a welfare state.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 658 Tm
(Classified into: 1. Socialistic Principles \(Art 38 welfare promotion, Art 39) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 643 Tm
(equitable distribution of resources, Art 39A equal justice and free legal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(aid\); 2. Gandhian Principles \(Art 40 Village Panchayats, Art 43 cottage) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(industries, Art 46 SC/ST educational interests, Art 47 prohibition of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 598 Tm
(intoxicating drinks\); 3. Liberal-Intellectual Principles \(Art 44 Uniform) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 583 Tm
(Civil Code, Art 45 early childhood care, Art 48 agriculture/animal) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 568 Tm
(husbandry, Art 48A environment protection, Art 50 separation of judiciary) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 553 Tm
(from executive, Art 51 international peace\).) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(In Minerva Mills \(1980\), the Supreme Court held that the Indian Constitution) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 516 Tm
(is founded on the bedrock of the balance between Part III \(Fundamental) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 501 Tm
(Rights\) and Part IV \(DPSPs\).) Tj
