1 0 0 1 50 725 Tm
(Basic Structure Doctrine & Amendment Power \(Article 368\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.15 rg
1 0 0 1 50 695 Tm
(Article 368 in Part XX empowers Parliament to amend the Constitution by) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 680 Tm
(special majority \(2/3 present & voting + majority of total membership\) or) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 665 Tm
(special majority with ratification by half of the states.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 643 Tm
(In Shankari Prasad \(1951\) and Sajjan Singh \(1965\), Parliament’s amending) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 628 Tm
(power was held unlimited. In Golak Nath \(1967\), the Court reversed this,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 613 Tm
(declaring Fundamental Rights could not be abridged.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 591 Tm
(The landmark 13-judge bench in Kesavananda Bharati \(1973\) formulated the) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 576 Tm
(Basic Structure Doctrine: Parliament can amend any part of the Constitution) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 561 Tm
(including Fundamental Rights, provided the basic structure \(Supremacy of) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 546 Tm
(Constitution, Republican & Democratic nature, Secularism, Federalism,) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 531 Tm
(Judicial Review\) remains intact.) Tj
ET
